{title: Holy Spirit, Truth Divine}
{artist: Samuel Longfellow / Orlando Gibbons}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{tempo: 107}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 456)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Holy Spir[G]it, [A]truth di[D]vine,
[A]Dawn upon [D]this [E]soul of [A]mine;
[D]Word of [A]God and [Em]inward [A]light
[A]Wake [D]my [A]spir[Bm]it, [Em]clear [A]my [D]sight.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Holy Spir[G]it, [A]love di[D]vine,
[A]Glow within [D]this [E]heart of [A]mine;
[D]Kindle [A]every [Em]high de[A]sire;
[A]Pe[D]rish [A]self [Bm]in [Em]Thy [A]pure [D]fire.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]Holy Spir[G]it, [A]joy di[D]vine,
[A]Gladden Thou [D]this [E]heart of [A]mine;
[D]In the [A]desert [Em]ways I [A]sing,
[A]Spring, [D]O [A]well, [Bm]for[Em]ev[A]er [D]spring.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[D]Now incline [G]me [A]to re[D]pent,
[A]Let me now [D]my [E]sins la[A]ment,
[D]Now my [A]foul re[Em]volt de[A]plore,
[A]Weep, [D]be[A]lieve, [Bm]and [Em]sin [A]no [D]more.
{end_of_verse}
